{"body":"## Bug\n\n`unseed --release X <CID>` correctly retracts the `radiroh://` location from release X's COB, but the node call underneath — `NodeMsg::Unseed { rid, cid }` — deletes the single shared `(rid, cid)` seeder tag for the whole repo.\n\nIf two releases in the same repo share an artifact (same CID), unseeding it from release X also stops seeding it for release Y. The bytes get GC'd on the next sweep; release Y's published location becomes unreachable.\n\n### Where the bug lives\n\n`node.rs:527-529` — `unseed_artifact` always sends `Unseed { rid, cid }` regardless of `--release`:\n\n```rust\nlet receipt = client\n    .call_blocking::<UnseedReceipt>(&NodeMsg::Unseed { rid, cid }, ...)\n    .map_err(client_err)?;\n```\n\n`seeder/mod.rs:149-158` — one tag per `(rid, cid)`, not one per `(rid, release, cid)`:\n\n```\n[SEEDED_TAG_V1][rid_len: u8][rid_bytes][CID binary]\n```\n\n## Paths forward\n\n### Path A — `(rid, release_id, cid)` key (additive change)\n\nExtend the binary tag key to include the release ID:\n\n```\n[SEEDED_TAG_V1][rid_len: u8][rid_bytes][release_id_bytes][cid_bytes]\n```\n\nOne tag per (repo, release, artifact). CID is in both key and value — a deliberate denormalization for O(1) per-artifact lookup. Unseeding a release becomes a prefix scan over `[V1][rid_len][rid_bytes][release_id_bytes]` and deleting all hits; no cross-checking of other releases needed.\n\nImpact: binary tag format breaks (pre-release; no migration needed). `seeded_tag`, `seeded_rid_prefix`, `parse_seeded_tag`, `tag_seeded`, `seed_artifact`, `is_seeded`, `unregister_seeded`, and callers in `node/mod.rs` change. The per-artifact wire protocol (`Command::Seed`, `Command::Fetch`) and `seed_to_release` stay the same.\n\n### Path B — per-release iroh collections (model change)\n\nSeal each release's artifact set into a single hash-seq collection at seed time:\n\n```\n(rid, release_id) → HashAndFormat::hash_seq(release_root)\n```\n\nOne tag per release. GC walks the hash-seq root to keep child artifact hashes alive; if artifact A appears in two release collections, both roots must be gone before GC reclaims it. CID not in the tag key.\n\nImpact: seeding becomes release-atomic — all artifacts must be known upfront. The per-artifact `Command::Seed` API would need a `Command::SeedRelease` counterpart. Larger scope, cleaner tag store.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nPath A is the lower-risk fix: it closes the isolation bug, keeps the existing per-artifact wire protocol, and the tag format change is safe pre-release.","type":"comment"}